FRESH REPOSITORY BASELINE

This repository intentionally starts a new scanner history from the packaged 200-item A+B baseline.

Meaning:
- Do NOT recover or require scanner-run history from commits that pre-date this fresh baseline.
- Do NOT require a pre-existing ab_archive or old Strand C history on the first run.
- Legacy version-specific regression tests from an older repository are not part of this repository contract.
- The normal scanner security boundary remains active: only radar.json may be persisted by the main scanner.

The actual one-time bootstrap state is the fresh_repository_seed marker inside radar.json.
After the first successful scan, that JSON marker is omitted from scanner output, so subsequent scans are normal incremental scans.
This file may remain in the repository as a permanent declaration that legacy repository-history contracts do not apply.
